From: Vendomat Fork <vendomat-fork@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] vendomat: inherit the inputs of an imported source's
 devenv.yaml

devenv ignores the `devenv.yaml` of a source that `imports` names by
input, as in `imports: [lib-b/devenv]`. A consumer must repeat every
input that the source declares.

Before the lock check, lock the consumer inputs in memory (virtual
mode) and read the pinned reference of each imported input. Fetch it
with `builtins.fetchTree` and read `<import dir>/devenv.yaml`. Add the
`inputs` of that file to the consumer inputs. Follow the input-style
`imports` of that file the same way, until no new import appears. Then
lock once and use the merged inputs for the bootstrap arguments and for
`devenv update`.

Also import the modules that a source lists in its own `imports`,
after the consumer's imports. A local import inside a source, such as
`./sub` in `lib-b/devenv`, becomes `lib-b/devenv/sub`. A local import
that leaves its input fails.

Conflict rule: an input that the consumer declares wins. `nixpkgs` and
`devenv` count as declared, because devenv adds a default for each. Two
sources must declare the same input identically, or the merge fails and
names both imports. A source input with a relative path URL fails.

Also build nested input overrides at any depth. Before, only one level
reached Nix and a deeper `follows` was dropped without a message. A
nested input that has neither url nor follows cannot reach Nix through
the C API, so it now fails with a message that names its path.

Upstream: cachix/devenv PR #3055 and issue #2205 (open on 2026-10-10)
cover the inheritance with a similar lock-read-relock loop. On v2.4.0
the PR fails for non-path sources and has no conflict error. Drop the
inheritance part when a pinned upstream release carries both.
